utions of higher education for students in early childhood education programs, requiring service in licensed early learning programs.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Child Care Workforce Development Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3273"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":9,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr3274-119","introducedDate":"2025-05-08","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-05-08","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 3274","policyArea":"Families","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Establishes infrastructure grants to states and intermediary organizations to help child care providers acquire, construct, renovate, or improve child care facilities, with priority given to facilities serving low-income populations and infants/toddlers. Requires needs assessments and Davis-Bacon wage standards for construction work.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Child Care Infrastructure Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3274"}],"state":"MA","topCrossPartyCollaborators":[]}
